@lang en
IMPORT prelude

-- "Assessed value" and the conversion of tax rates: Gov. Code § 25.
--
-- Added in pass 2 of the completion to "whole".  Pass 1 called this section "not applicable" as property-tax arithmetic; the brief has no such disposition,
-- and the section defines a term ("assessed value") and states two conversion factors, which are computed here.
-- The quotation lines are copied by script from the converter-made plain-text rendering of the section (not the official text) and checked against it by srcrefs.py.
-- Target: unstable (REFUSE).  Imports: prelude only.
--
-- A fiscal year is given by the first calendar year in its name: 1980 for the 1980-81 fiscal year.  The text says "fiscal year" and does not say when one begins
-- or ends, and nothing here depends on that.  "Full value" is not defined in the deposited text (it is a term of the property tax), so it is a number the caller supplies.
--
-- Fork F-25c: a rate "expressed as a percentage of full value" is read as the fraction of full value that percentage stands for (1 percent is 0.01).
-- Only that reading makes the two factors of subdivision (c) agree: 0.0025 (twenty-five hundredths of 1 percent) times 400 is 1.  Read as the figure 1 (for 1 percent),
-- the second factor would turn a rate of $4 on each $100 into 400 instead of back into 4.  The same factors fall out of subdivision (b), which asks for the same tax revenue.

§ `Gov. Code § 25(a): assessed value and the way tax rates are expressed`

DECLARE `Way a tax rate is expressed` IS ONE OF
    `dollars, or fractions thereof, on each one hundred dollars ($100) of assessed value`
    `a percentage of full value`

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:92 | 25. (a) For purposes of this code, “assessed value” means 25 percent of full value to, and including, the 1980–81 fiscal year, and 100 percent of full value for the 1981–82 fiscal year and fiscal years thereafter; and, tax rates shall be expressed in dollars, or fractions thereof, on each one hundred dollars ($100) of assessed value to, and including, the 1980–81 fiscal year and as a percentage of full value for the 1981–82 fiscal year and fiscal years thereafter.
@ref Gov. Code § 25(a) (src:GOV-ss-1-26:92)
GIVEN `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the percent of full value that assessed value is in the fiscal year` `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year` MEANS
    IF `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year` LESS THAN 1981
    THEN 25
    ELSE 100

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:92 | 25. (a) For purposes of this code, “assessed value” means 25 percent of full value to, and including, the 1980–81 fiscal year, and 100 percent of full value for the 1981–82 fiscal year and fiscal years thereafter; and, tax rates shall be expressed in dollars, or fractions thereof, on each one hundred dollars ($100) of assessed value to, and including, the 1980–81 fiscal year and as a percentage of full value for the 1981–82 fiscal year and fiscal years thereafter.
@ref Gov. Code § 25(a) (src:GOV-ss-1-26:92)
GIVEN `the full value of the property` IS A NUMBER
      `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the assessed value of property whose full value is` `the full value of the property` `in the fiscal year` `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year` MEANS
    `the full value of the property` TIMES `the percent of full value that assessed value is in the fiscal year` `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year` DIVIDED BY 100

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:92 | 25. (a) For purposes of this code, “assessed value” means 25 percent of full value to, and including, the 1980–81 fiscal year, and 100 percent of full value for the 1981–82 fiscal year and fiscal years thereafter; and, tax rates shall be expressed in dollars, or fractions thereof, on each one hundred dollars ($100) of assessed value to, and including, the 1980–81 fiscal year and as a percentage of full value for the 1981–82 fiscal year and fiscal years thereafter.
@ref Gov. Code § 25(a) (src:GOV-ss-1-26:92)
GIVEN `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Way a tax rate is expressed`
`the way tax rates are expressed in the fiscal year` `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year` MEANS
    IF `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year` LESS THAN 1981
    THEN `dollars, or fractions thereof, on each one hundred dollars ($100) of assessed value`
    ELSE `a percentage of full value`

§ `Gov. Code § 25(b): comparisons for different years are made on the same basis`

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:93 | (b) Whenever this code requires comparison of assessed values, tax rates, or property tax revenues for different years, the assessment ratios and tax rates shall be adjusted as necessary so that the comparisons are made on the same basis, and the same amount of tax revenues would be produced, or the same relative value of an exemption or subvention will be realized regardless of the method of expressing tax rates or the assessment ratio utilized.
@ref Gov. Code § 25(b) (src:GOV-ss-1-26:93)
-- An amount measured in assessed value (an assessed value, or an exemption stated as an amount of assessed value) is restated so that it stands for the same part of
-- the property's full value in the other year: from a 25 percent year to a 100 percent year it is multiplied by 4, and back, divided by 4.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year it is measured in` IS A NUMBER
      `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year it is compared with` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`an amount of assessed value restated for comparison` amount `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year it is measured in` `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year it is compared with` MEANS
    amount
        TIMES `the percent of full value that assessed value is in the fiscal year` `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year it is compared with`
        DIVIDED BY `the percent of full value that assessed value is in the fiscal year` `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year it is measured in`

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:93 | (b) Whenever this code requires comparison of assessed values, tax rates, or property tax revenues for different years, the assessment ratios and tax rates shall be adjusted as necessary so that the comparisons are made on the same basis, and the same amount of tax revenues would be produced, or the same relative value of an exemption or subvention will be realized regardless of the method of expressing tax rates or the assessment ratio utilized.
@ref Gov. Code § 25(b) (src:GOV-ss-1-26:93)
-- A tax rate is restated so that "the same amount of tax revenues would be produced".  A rate in dollars on each $100 of assessed value, in a year when assessed value
-- is 25 percent of full value, produces r / 100 x (25 / 100) of full value in tax, that is 0.0025 r of full value; and a rate that is a fraction p of full value
-- produces p of it, which is 400 p dollars on each $100 of assessed value at 25 percent.  A rate in a year of the same expression is unchanged.
GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER
      `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year it is expressed in` IS A NUMBER
      `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year it is compared with` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`a tax rate restated for comparison` rate `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year it is expressed in` `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year it is compared with` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   `the way tax rates are expressed in the fiscal year` `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year it is expressed in`
             EQUALS `the way tax rates are expressed in the fiscal year` `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year it is compared with`
            THEN rate
        IF `the first calendar year in the name of the fiscal year it is expressed in` LESS THAN 1981
            THEN rate TIMES (25 DIVIDED BY 10000)
        OTHERWISE rate TIMES 400

§ `Gov. Code § 25(c): the two conversion factors`

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:94 | (c) For purposes of expressing tax rates on the same basis, a tax rate based on a 25 percent assessment ratio and expressed in dollars, or fractions thereof, for each one hundred dollars ($100) of assessed value may be multiplied by a conversion factor of twenty-five hundredths of 1 percent to determine a rate comparable to a rate expressed as a percentage of full value; and, a rate expressed as a percentage of full value may be multiplied by a factor of 400 to determine a rate comparable to a rate expressed in dollars, or fractions thereof, for each one hundred dollars ($100) of assessed value and based on a 25 percent assessment ratio.
@ref Gov. Code § 25(c) (src:GOV-ss-1-26:94)
-- "may be multiplied by a conversion factor of twenty-five hundredths of 1 percent": 25/100 of 1/100.
GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`a rate in dollars on each $100 of assessed value at a 25 percent assessment ratio, restated as comparable to a percentage of full value` rate MEANS
    rate TIMES ((25 DIVIDED BY 100) TIMES (1 DIVIDED BY 100))

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:94 | (c) For purposes of expressing tax rates on the same basis, a tax rate based on a 25 percent assessment ratio and expressed in dollars, or fractions thereof, for each one hundred dollars ($100) of assessed value may be multiplied by a conversion factor of twenty-five hundredths of 1 percent to determine a rate comparable to a rate expressed as a percentage of full value; and, a rate expressed as a percentage of full value may be multiplied by a factor of 400 to determine a rate comparable to a rate expressed in dollars, or fractions thereof, for each one hundred dollars ($100) of assessed value and based on a 25 percent assessment ratio.
@ref Gov. Code § 25(c) (src:GOV-ss-1-26:94)
-- "may be multiplied by a factor of 400": the rate is the fraction of full value that the percentage stands for (fork F-25c).
GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`a rate expressed as a percentage of full value, restated as comparable to dollars on each $100 of assessed value at a 25 percent assessment ratio` rate MEANS
    rate TIMES 400
